# EcoSpark — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored; never commit it,
# never paste real keys into source, logs, screenshots, or issue threads.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT — two classes of variable live in this file
#
#   VITE_*  are inlined into the browser bundle at build time. They are PUBLIC.
#           Anyone can read them from the shipped JS. Only put values here that
#           are safe to disclose, and protect them at the provider instead
#           (Firebase security rules, HTTP referrer restrictions, quotas).
#
#   others  are read only by serverless functions in `api/` and never reach the
#           client. Real secrets belong here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ Firebase — client SDK ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Public by design. A Firebase web API key is an identifier, not a secret; access
# is controlled by firestore.rules. Restrict it by HTTP referrer in the Google
# Cloud console anyway.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-web-api-key
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:0000000000000000000000


# ═══ Firebase Admin — serverless only ════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRET. Grants full read/write to the project, bypassing all security rules.
# From a service-account JSON: Firebase console → Project settings →
# Service accounts → Generate new private key.
#
# FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY must keep its literal \n escapes and stay quoted — the
# code un-escapes them (api/_lib/firebaseAdmin.js).
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nREPLACE_WITH_YOUR_KEY\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"


# ═══ AI providers — server side ══════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRET. Used by api/verify.js (Gemini Vision task proof) and api/coach.js
# (Groq-streamed coach).
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key


# ═══ News ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Used by api/news.js to proxy real eco/climate headlines from GNews.io.
GNEWS_API_KEY=your-gnews-api-key


# ═══ Cron ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRET. Shared bearer token that authenticates Vercel Cron calls to
# api/streak-reset.js. Generate a long random value, e.g.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
CRON_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string


# ═══ Legacy client-side AI keys — being retired ══════════════════════════════
# These ship in the browser bundle and are therefore effectively public. They
# exist because src/services/aiService.js currently calls Gemini/Groq directly
# from the client to dodge Vercel's serverless timeout (see docs/regalia-audit.md,
# finding A-5). Prefer the server-side keys above; leave these unset once the
# corresponding call sites have been moved behind `api/`.
#
# If you do set them, use SEPARATE, tightly quota-limited keys — not the same
# values as GEMINI_API_KEY / GROQ_API_KEY above.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=
VITE_GNEWS_API_KEY=
